OL,3,GNEWSAAre the autumns we remember
OL,4,Adisappearing?
OL,5,
OL,6,FFrosty Halloween mornings. Bonfire
OL,7,FNight wrapped up in hats and gloves.
OL,8,FTrees turning red, orange and gold.
OL,10,FFor many of us, those are the hallmarks
OL,11,Fof a traditional autumn.
OL,13,FYet as October draws to a close, with
OL,14,Fleaves still clinging to branches and
OL,15,Fpatches of green lingering in parks and
OL,16,Fwoodlands, some people are asking what
OL,17,Fhappened to the autumn they remember.
OL,23,APub: 31-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,355,350,200,160,0,100
